;; FH-REACT-001 — the outward bridge takes a declared view, and one option.
;;
;; The whole value of exporting a DESCRIPTOR rather than a function is that the
;; thing React ends up holding still has a qualified id, a source coordinate and
;; a lowering — so a failure inside a foreign library's subtree names the view,
;; and a hot reload has something stable to reload into. A bridge that accepted
;; any callable would hand React an opaque closure and throw all of that away at
;; exactly the boundary where it is least recoverable.
;;
;; `:rejected` is therefore spelled as the four shapes a caller actually reaches
;; for — the view's OWN id keyword and a rendered form are the two near-misses,
;; and both classify as "not a descriptor" rather than as some softer thing.
;;
;; The option roster is the second half of the row and is closed at one key. An
;; unknown option is REFUSED rather than ignored, because the failure mode of
;; ignoring is silent: a caller who writes `:map-props?` or `:props-mapper` gets
;; the default shallow rule and a subtly wrong render, with nothing anywhere
;; saying the option did not exist.
{:fh/id "FH-REACT-001"
 :fh/law
 "The outward bridge exports a DECLARED view and nothing else — a plain function, a hiccup vector, a view id keyword and a rendered form are each refused naming a declared view or an explicit wrapper as the recovery — and its option roster is closed at the single `:map-props` adapter, which must be a function: an unknown option is refused rather than ignored."

 ;; The one diagnostic every refusal on this row carries.
 :error :rf.error/ui-tree-malformed

 ;; What a declared view answers with: a real React component type, and a
 ;; displayName naming the view rather than an anonymous wrapper.
 :accepted
 {:view-id      :re-frame.freehand.to-react-views/person-cell
  :display-name "v/->react(:re-frame.freehand.to-react-views/person-cell)"}

 ;; Not descriptors. Each names what a caller plausibly passed instead.
 :rejected
 [{:note "a plain function — the shape a wrapper-writer reaches for"
   :kind :fn
   :recovery :export-a-declared-view-or-write-a-wrapper}
  {:note "a hiccup vector — markup, not a view"
   :kind :vector
   :recovery :export-a-declared-view-or-write-a-wrapper}
  {:note "the view's own id keyword — the nearest miss there is"
   :kind :keyword
   :recovery :export-a-declared-view-or-write-a-wrapper}
  {:note "a rendered form — the view already mounted"
   :kind :rendered
   :recovery :export-a-declared-view-or-write-a-wrapper}]

 ;; The closed option roster.
 :options
 {:roster   [:map-props]
  :accepted {:note "the one adapter, a function of the foreign props object"}
  :rejected
  [{:note     "an unknown option is refused, never ignored"
    :opts     {:map-porps :fn}
    :recovery :use-map-props-or-write-a-wrapper}
   {:note     "the adapter must be a function"
    :opts     {:map-props :not-a-fn}
    :recovery :supply-a-one-argument-function}
   {:note     "the options slot is a map"
    :opts     :not-a-map
    :recovery :supply-an-options-map}]}}
